  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x8CB4" flags="0x0">
    <title>Filter Target Additive Correction (0xAB0A)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0xAB0A; 8 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Interpolated 8x8 uint8 table with output in the range 4..37. Its output is a separate correction term: uint8 from ffff1071 is added, the sum is centered by subtracting 0x32, and the result is multiplied by uint8 from ffff3502. ffff3502 carries the output of adjacent map 0000b23a, which contains only value 27, rather than the target map's output. The resulting product conditionally participates in updating 32-bit ffff2d20; code does not establish a physical name or unit. Interpolated 8x8 uint8 table with output in the range 4..37. Its output is a separate correction term: uint8 from ffff1071 is added, the sum is centered by subtracting 0x32, and the result is multiplied by uint8 from ffff3502. ffff3502 carries the output of adjacent map 0000b23a, which contains only value 27, rather than the target map's output. The resulting product conditionally participates in updating 32-bit ffff2d20; code does not establish a physical name or unit. Result disposition: consumer. Result target: FUN_000befb0@000befb0: when bit 3 in ffff41bc is set and uint8@ffff3502 is nonzero, expression (uint8@ffff1071 + map_output - 0x32) * uint8@ffff3502 participates through sign-dependent arithmetic in forming the 32-bit value written to ffff2d20. Machine trace: 0000ab0a (8x8 uint8, values 4..37) -&gt; base load into r4 at 000befe0, axes 000120ae/000120b6 and raw inputs from the high byte of ffff1024 and byte ffff11ae -&gt; call 00026140 at 000beff4 -&gt; kernel passes 00026944 and raw-cell selection in 00026770 -&gt; unsigned linear interpolation 00026740, which keeps the result between adjacent uint8 values -&gt; r0 -&gt; r6 -&gt; byte write to ffff3219 at 000beffe. This result remains separate from the previous call's result: the previous call interpolates adjacent map 0000b23a and writes its output to ffff3502. Then, when (ffff41bc &amp; 8) != 0, code reads ffff3502 at 000bf024 and, if it is nonzero after the check at 000bf02a, calculates (uint8@ffff1071 + map_output - 0x32) * uint8@ffff3502. The resulting term is combined with a quantity derived from ffff2d24 relative to 0x32000000, including signed branches and bounds, and the result is written to ffff2d20. When bit 3 is clear, only initialization of ffff2d20 from ffff106e occurs; when ffff3502 is zero, the arithmetic branch is skipped.</description>
