  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x5E29" flags="0x0">
    <title>Filter Weight - new-sample share Q16 (0xB23A)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0xB23A; 8 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. First-order lag-filter smoothing coefficient, meaning the weight of the new sample: new = old*(65536-K)/65536 + target*K/65536. K=0 disables updating; the physical quantity is unknown. First-order lag-filter smoothing coefficient, meaning the weight of the new sample: new = old*(65536-K)/65536 + target*K/65536. K=0 disables updating; the physical quantity is unknown. Result disposition: consumer. Result target: FUN_000befb0@000bf024, final write to RAM ffff2d20. Machine trace: 0000b23a -&gt; 000befc4/000befd8 -&gt; 00026140 -&gt; 00026944/00026c78 -&gt; 00026770/00026740 -&gt; 000befe2 -&gt; ffff3502 -&gt; 000bf024/000bf028/000bf02a -&gt; FUN_000befb0 -&gt; ffff2d20. Scale confidence: code. Scale: x/65536; inverse encoding: x*65536; units: new-sample fraction (0..255/65536). Scale trace: 0000b23a -&gt; 000befd8 -&gt; 00026140 -&gt; 00026944/00026c78 -&gt; 00026770/00026740 -&gt; r0 -&gt; 000befe2(ffff3502) -&gt; 000bf024 -&gt; FUN_000befb0 arithmetic: u=uint8; with u=0 the update is skipped, otherwise the old Q8.24 deviation is multiplied by (0x10000-u)/0x10000 and the byte input deviation is multiplied by u*0x100. Signed branches add or subtract these parts, restore the value relative to 0x32000000, and saturate the result -&gt; ffff2d20/ffff2d24 -&gt; high byte ffff359c.</description>
