  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xFA55" flags="0x0">
    <title>Throttle Rev Limiter (0x942C)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x942C; 1 rows x 1 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Calibrated upper rotational-speed threshold in a throttle-control limiter path. FUN 0002c648 copies the scalar to ffff1796 during initialization. FUN 0007584e treats 0xffff as disabled, converts current speed ffff11b6 into the same internal domain by multiplying it by four, rate-limits the threshold state, and writes signed candidate ffff19d8. FUN 00071508 includes ffff19d8 in a signed minimum cascade that writes ffff243a. Scheduler 000702a0 runs the downstream controller stages; FUN 00070d82 selects ffff243a or controller result ffff19c0 and publishes the same signed value as ffff2438 and ffff19c2. FUN 00079030 applies additional signed bounds and writes ffff19c6, which enters the interpolation path through FUN 00073432. An independent use in FUN 00077892 caps a derived uint16 at 0x942c, applies lower bound 0x94b2, and writes ffff32ec; this auxiliary branch has no assigned physical semantics. The stock word is 0x2580, or 7500 RPM with the HR A2L multiplier. Public EV18A definitions place Throttle Rev Limiter at 0x9478 and Speed Limiter at 0x94c2; the corresponding JK08A limiter scalars are 0x942c and 0x9476, preserving a -0x4c layout offset for both anchors. The adjacent JK08A speed branch writes ffff19de into the same signed minimum cascade. Working fuel-cut table 0000934e has candidate Normal activation and release values of 7650 and 7450 RPM, placing the 7500 RPM throttle setting between them. Exact code closes the limiter path through the shared signed airflow/torque-request coordinate ffff19c6, but no continuous trace reaches a bank-specific throttle-angle command, motor PWM register, or ECM terminal. The physical label and multiplier remain catalog/homology evidence pending a controlled hardware test.</description>
