    <title>Constant Output 255 - raw u8 (0x120BE)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x120BE; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. Physical semantics are unknown; a constant 1D table produces raw byte 255 for RAM ffff2ea2. All 16 elements equal 0xff, so the written raw byte is 255 for any index. This constant alone does not prove a limit role, threshold role, or physical quantity. The call and write are in a branch that tests bit 4 through ffff24b8; after execution, the bit is set at site 00039a18. Branch unreachability has not been proven, so the map is not dead. The catalog contains several incompatible 1D-16 uint8 classes and does not identify the map by shape or contents. Blocking condition: The trace stops at RAM ffff2ea2 after the write at site 00039a10: ffff2ea2 has no external readers, and inside 0003995a the target-map result is not compared, returned, or used in another consuming operation. Physical semantics therefore cannot be established from code. Result disposition: writes.</description>
