    <title>Conditional Parameter High Byte - raw u8 (0x120F6)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x120F6; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. Physical semantics are unknown; code defines a conditionally selected high byte of a composite 16-bit parameter obtained by 1D interpolation using input ffff110e. All 16 cells equal 60, so the index does not change the result, but a flat constant does not establish its purpose. The result is stored at 0004ff42 and, on a reachable conditional branch, loaded at 0004ff6c into the high byte of a returned uint16. Caller 0004ed88 first stores the word in ffff9f34, copies its high byte to ffff14bd, and passes the word to 000503e0. The catalog contains several incompatible classes and scales for 1D-16 uint8, so no unique identification exists. Blocking condition: The map result reaches 000503e0 only as the high byte of a composite third argument; the artifact lacks the consumer body or contract that would establish the physical meaning of this byte, so semantics and physical scale remain unknown. Result disposition: consumer.</description>
