  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xA1BE" flags="0x0">
    <title>Conditional Triple-Product Multiplier - raw u8 (0x12282)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12282; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. Branch-selected interpolated uint8 multiplier participates in calculating sat_u16(uint8(ffff2f94) * uint16(v) * uint8(out) &gt;&gt; 14). The target branch loads 00012282 at 000b212c, calls the wrapper at 000b2132, and writes a byte to ffff2f8d at 000b213c. On the alternate branch, the same RAM register receives the result of adjacent 000122b2; this trace applies only to the target branch. Common block LAB_000b227e reads ffff2f8d, includes the value in an unsigned product with byte ffff2f94 and a 16-bit intermediate quantity, shifts the full product right by 14, limits the result to 0xffff, and writes it through param_3. Caller 000b29b8 binds param_3 to ffff301c. The value is not dead. The shared shift by 14 does not distribute fractional bits unambiguously between the two byte multipliers, so a separate x/128 scale is not claimed for this map. Blocking condition: In caller 000b29b8, only reads of the high byte of derived 16-bit result ffff301c, comparisons with unnamed ROM thresholds, and flag changes are visible; the physical consumer and physical quantity are unknown. Promotion rejected: Target attribution is confirmed: 000b212c loads address 00012282, the call at 000b2132 passes it to wrapper 00026388, and 000b213c writes the low result byte to ffff2f8d. The alternate branch writes the result of 000122b2 there, so conditional map selection is distinguished. Passing the array into lookup and byte loads in the kernel confirm role=table. C pseudocode for 000b2096 shows matching arithmetic: uint8(ffff2f94) * (uVar4 &amp; 0xffff) * uint8(ffff2f8d) &gt;&gt; 14 with saturation to 0xffff; the local read of the target-map result confirms disposition=consumer. However, code confidence fails the complete machine-trace requirement: unannotated kernel 00026a84 ends by branching into finisher 00026740, whose listing and contract are absent, while the final multiplications, shift, and saturation are shown only in C pseudocode without machine listing. Wrapper 00026388 also has an endpoint branch that returns the last cell directly, so the literal characterization of the result as always interpolated is not proven. Semantics and evidence sufficiency are therefore refuted under the stated conservative rule. No separate scale is claimed; raw identity requires no scale evidence. Result disposition: consumer.</description>
