  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xA5E3" flags="0x0">
    <title>High-range Quotient Divisor - raw u16 (0x15022)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x15022; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. High-range branch of a piecewise denominator table: the high byte of interpolated uint16 is tested for zero and, when nonzero, used as divisor in unsigned quotient (ffff1737 &lt;&lt; 8) / value. Code establishes operational rather than physical semantics. The interpolation result is quantized as (r0 &gt;&gt; 8) &amp; 0xff, written to ffff1738, and used through the same r6 without reading RAM. ffff1738 has no external readers, but the flow is not dead: r6 is tested for zero and becomes divisor 00021ce0 on the nonzero branch; the zero branch forms 0xff. No physical quantity or engineering unit follows from this consumption. Loss of the low 8 bits has no exact inverse, so only raw identity is claimed. Result disposition: consumer.</description>
