    <title>Initial Retard Quantity - unresolved mode (0x1202E)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x1202E; 1 rows x 4 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. Candidate of the Initial Retard Quantity Table family: initial ignition-retard quantity for transient correction; the specific operating-mode variant is unknown. Code proves a conditional unsigned 1D-4 lookup: when (RAM ffff2459 &amp; 0x20)==0, the accessor constrains the index to 0..255, interpolates uint8 nodes, and copies the byte result into two RAM regions. All four cells equal 200, so every executed lookup writes 200. The catalog match establishes only a candidate for the general family and units, without an address or concept association. Index: x = min(max((uint16_t)r5 - 96, 0), 255). Implicit nodes are located at x=0, 64, 128, 192: for x&lt;192, i=x/64 and Q0.16 fraction (x-i*64)*1024 are used; for x&gt;=192, element 3 is returned. Result disposition: writes (RAM ffff1ee0 at site 0003e2da; RAM ffff257a at site 0003e2de). Blocking condition: The machine trace ends after writes 0003e2da/ffff1ee0 and 0003e2de/ffff257a: the artifact contains no external readers of either register and no consumer associated with the lookup result. The six shown consumers read ffff4226, which is not a sink for the map result. Therefore, code does not establish physical semantics or distinguish the five operating-mode variants in the catalog.</description>
