  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x8C31" flags="0x0">
    <title>Four-Factor Product Multiplier B Q0.8 (0x11E56)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x11E56; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. One of three unsigned table multipliers applied to base byte ffff1294. Its interpolated result participates in a four-factor product; the normalized result is written to ffff22f8 and controls bit 0 of ffff2473 according to whether it is zero. The artifact does not identify the physical subsystem. The lookup result is stored in ffff1296 and reread locally; ffff1296 has no external readers. ffff1294 is the base byte, while ffff1295, ffff1296, and ffff1297 are three Q0.8 multipliers: floor(ffff1294*ffff1295*ffff1296*ffff1297/2^24) is written to ffff22f8. A zero result clears bit 0 of ffff2473, while a nonzero result sets it. Numeric round trip for ROM value 13: (13/256)*256=13. Index: Implicit uniform 1D-8 axis: u=min((uint16[ffff1024]&gt;&gt;7),255); for u&lt;224, i=u&gt;&gt;5 and a Q0.16 fraction from the low 5 bits interpolate cells[i] and cells[i+1]; for u&gt;=224, cells[7] is returned. Result disposition: consumer (0004b9b4@0004ba18).</description>
