    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12096; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Unsigned 1D table of the second multiplier in a composite calculation. The interpolated byte is stored in ffff1451 and, at site 0004c34c, multiplied by low32(r12 * lookup(0001208e)); low32 of the product is passed as a signed 32-bit dividend to 00021bbc, divided by 0x14000 with truncation toward zero, capped at 255 by an unsigned comparison, and written as a byte to ffff1875. The physical quantities of input ffff1450 and the coefficient are unknown. There is no separate ROM axis: indexing is implicit, so axes is empty. ffff1451 has no external readers, but the saved copy of the result in r5 is consumed inside the accessor at site 0004c34c; the value is not dead. A nontrivial scale for the individual multiplier cannot be separated from the composite product with 0001208e and r12. Index: x=uint8(RAM[ffff1450]); for x&gt;=224, cell[7] is returned; otherwise i=x&gt;&gt;5, f=(x&amp;31)&lt;&lt;11 in Q0.16, and the result is unsigned linear interpolation of cell[i] and cell[i+1]. Result disposition: consumer (site 0004c34c).</description>
