  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x3518" flags="0x0">
    <title>Dual-Lookup Additive Correction (0x120CE)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x120CE; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Implicit eight-point byte-correction table. The accessor combines two linearly interpolated results of this map as (lookup@00068d08 + lookup@00068d3a - 128)*8 and writes the value as signed16 to ffff2018. Consumer 00068d58 adds the correction to the result of unsigned division 00021ce0, constrains the sum to range 125..(u16[ffff201a]-125), and writes the result to ffff201e. The physical name and unit of the quantity are unknown. Code does not define a single decoding scale for an individual cell: offset 128 applies only to the second lookup result, while multiplication by 8 occurs after the two results are added. The map has no addressable axes, so axes is empty. Index: Implicit 1D-8 with a byte selector and linear interpolation: for selector &lt;224, 00026370 passes calculation to 00026a80/00026740; for selector &gt;=224, it returns cell 7. Site 00068d08 uses the byte after an arithmetic right shift by 7 through 000224f8; site 00068d3a uses clamp(u16[ffff2020]-144,0,255). Result disposition: consumer (ffff2018 -&gt; 00068d58 -&gt; ffff201e).</description>
