  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x60F9" flags="0x0">
    <title>Triple-Product Multiplier A - raw u8 (0x1211E)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x1211E; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Unsigned 8-bit table multiplier M: lookup result 0001211e is stored in ffff14d8, then multiplied by the results of 0001212e and 00009d2a; the final value is calculated as min(255, (M*N*B)&gt;&gt;14) and written to ffff14d9. All eight cells equal 128, so in this ROM the lookup result does not depend on the index. ffff14d8 has no external readers, but the value is not dead: 0004ac7a reads it again and uses it in the product. Code does not establish the physical quantity or allocation of the common divisor 2^14 among the three multipliers, so the scale remains raw. Index: u=0 when U16[ffff18e2] &lt; 0x2000; u=floor((U16[ffff18e2]-0x2000)/64) when 0x2000 &lt;= U16[ffff18e2] &lt; 0x6000; u=255 when U16[ffff18e2] &gt;= 0x6000. u is passed as uint8; for u &gt;= 224, 00026370 returns cell[7]; otherwise it performs implicit 1D-8 interpolation of adjacent uint8 cells. Result disposition: consumer (ffff14d8 -&gt; 0004ac7a@0004ad60 -&gt; ffff14d9@0004ad7c).</description>
