  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x333A" flags="0x0">
    <title>Triple-Product Multiplier B Q0.7 (0x1212E)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x1212E; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Dimensionless 1D attenuation coefficient T selected by byte ffff106f. The interpolated result is read from ffff14db and serves as a multiplier in ffff14d9 = min(255, (T*A*B) &gt;&gt; 14), where A is in ffff14d8 and B is in ffff14da. The physical subsystem and the physical unit of input ffff106f are unknown. Quantity T is traced separately through ffff14db. In the current ROM, adjacent multiplier A from 0001211e is always 128, so the overall calculation reduces to floor(B*T/128), where B comes from 00009d2a. Saturation to 255 applies to the overall product. Numeric scale round trip: 102/128=0.796875, 0.796875*128=102; 128/128=1, 1*128=128. The implicit map has no explicit ROM axis, so axes is empty. Index: implicit 1D-8: u=uint8(ffff106f); for u&lt;224, index i=floor(u/32), fraction f=(u mod 32)/32, and cells i and i+1 are linearly interpolated; for u&gt;=224, cell 7 is returned. Result disposition: consumer (0004ad60).</description>
