  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xC731" flags="0x0">
    <title>Negative-Branch Multiplier Source - raw u8 (0x12176)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12176; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Eight-point table of an unsigned multiplier for the negative branch of signed16 ffff1a66: the interpolated map byte is divided by 2, written to ffff150a, and multiplied by ffff1a66 at 00052902; the product is divided by 256 with truncation toward zero, saturated to signed16, zeroed for a specified flag combination, and written to ffff2300. When ffff1a66 &gt;= 0, the map value is replaced with constant 64 before the write. The physical quantity is unknown. The map value affects the write to ffff150a only on path int16[ffff1a66] &lt; 0; when ffff1a66 &gt;= 0, the result register is replaced with constant 64. For map values 70..102, the map-derived byte after shar is 35..51. Conversion floor(x/2), subsequent multiplication, and division by 256 are conditional and do not form an exact invertible scale pair; in particular, x/512 does not correctly describe odd cells 77 and 93. Index: Implicit index: b=uint8[ffff102c]; q=(b&lt;128)?2*b:255. For q&gt;=224, equivalent to b&gt;=112, element 7 is selected; for q&lt;224, kernel 00026a80 reads adjacent uint8 values and passes them to Q0.16 interpolator 00026740. There is no explicit ROM axis; preparation of the exact index/fraction before the shown 00026a80 slice is not included in the artifact. Result disposition: writes (ffff150a).</description>
