  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xCA8E" flags="0x0">
    <title>Three-Factor Product Multiplier A - raw u8 (0x129CA)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x129CA; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Eight-point uint8 1D table of a multiplicative term in a composite calculation. Interpolated result x is zero-extended, multiplied by result y of map 00012dca and by 16-bit intermediate r14; the accessor calculates min(65535,(r14*x*y)&gt;&gt;14) and writes the result to ffff14dc. A copy of x is written to ffff179a. The physical subsystem is unknown. All 8 cells equal 128, so in this ROM the lookup always yields raw 128. This alone does not prove a unit or physical meaning. Code proves only the combined arithmetic min(65535,(r14*x*y)&gt;&gt;14), where x is the output of 000129ca and y is the output of 00012dca. Divisor 2^14 cannot be uniquely allocated among the scales of x, y, and r14 without an independent unit for one operand, so no separate nontrivial map scale is claimed. The map has no addressable axis, and its index grid is implicit. Index: implicit 1D-8 uint8. Selector extu.b(r12): r12=0 when uint16(ffff18e2)&lt;0x2000, r12=(uint16(ffff18e2)-0x2000)&gt;&gt;6 when 0x2000&lt;=uint16(ffff18e2)&lt;0x6000, otherwise r12=0xff. For selector &gt;=0xe0, wrapper 00026370 returns cell[7]; for a lower selector, kernel 00026a80 reads adjacent uint8 cells and finisher 00026740 performs unsigned linear interpolation. Output trace: 000129ca -&gt; site 0004ae20 -&gt; site 0004ae24 -&gt; 00026370 -&gt; 00026a80 -&gt; site 00026aac + site 00026aae -&gt; 00026740 -&gt; site 0004ae28 -&gt; [site 0004ae2c -&gt; ffff179a; site 0004ae2e -&gt; site 0004ae36 -&gt; site 0004ae3e -&gt; site 0004ae42 -&gt; site 0004ae44 -&gt; site 0004ae46 -&gt; site 0004ae48 -&gt; site 0004ae4a -&gt; site 0004ae4e -&gt; site 0004ae52 -&gt; ffff14dc]. Result disposition: consumer; Result target: site 0004ae36.</description>
