  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xD9DD" flags="0x0">
    <title>Paired Product Multiplier A - raw u8 (0x12A22)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12A22; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. On the enabled branch, the unsigned 1D-8 lookup result is used as one of two 8-bit factors: it is written to ffff17c7, zero-extended, and multiplied by byte ffff17c8, after which max(product, 0x4000) is written as uint16 to ffff19a4. The physical quantity and subsystem are not established: ffff17c7 has no external readers, while code proves the local multiplicative role. All 8 cells equal 128; this is not used as independent semantic evidence. There is no stored axis. Index: implicit 1D-8: z=min(floor(max(u16[ffff4524]-0x4600,0)/160),255). For z&lt;224, index i=floor(z/32), Q0.16 fraction equals (z mod 32)*2048; for z&gt;=224, element 7 is selected. Output trace: 000716f8(map 00012a22) -&gt; 000716fc(lookup) -&gt; 00026370 -&gt; [00026aac/00026aae -&gt; 00026740 for z&lt;224; element 7 for z&gt;=224] -&gt; 00071700(r0-&gt;r2) -&gt; 00071706(ffff17c7) -&gt; 00071708(r2 unsigned) -&gt; 00071710(MACL) -&gt; 00071716(r2) -&gt; 00071718 -&gt; 0007171c/0007171e -&gt; 00071722(ffff19a4). Result disposition: writes; Result target: ffff17c7.</description>
