  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xD993" flags="0x0">
    <title>Paired Product Multiplier B - raw u8 (0x12A2A)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12A2A; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. One of two unsigned 8-bit table multipliers: the interpolated output is multiplied by the output of map 00012a22, after which the product is lower-capped at 0x4000 and written to RAM ffff19a4. All 8 cells in the current image equal 128, so the lookup returns byte 128 for every q. Code proves only the operational multiplier role: the result is stored in ffff17c8, read again, and multiplied by the output of adjacent map 00012a22; the product is lower-capped at 0x4000 and written to ffff19a4. The physical subsystem and a nontrivial scale do not follow from the artifact. Index: q = min(max((u8[ffff10f4] - 80)*2, 0), 255); for q &lt; 224, wrapper 00026370 passes q to the linear-interpolation kernel for adjacent uint8 cells in the implicit 1D-8 grid; for q &gt;= 224, it returns cell 7. Output trace: 000716c0 -&gt; 000716c2 -&gt; 00026370 -&gt; 00026a80 -&gt; 00026aac -&gt; 00026aae -&gt; 00026740 -&gt; 000716c4 -&gt; 000716ca -&gt; ffff17c8 -&gt; 0007170c -&gt; 00071710 -&gt; 00071718 -&gt; 00071722 -&gt; ffff19a4 -&gt; 000718d8/00071a10/00071b7e. Result disposition: consumer; Result target: site 00071710.</description>
