  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x58" flags="0x0">
    <title>State Gate Byte Table - raw u8 (0x12A9A)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12A9A; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Implicit 1D-8 table of an unsigned byte over RAM ffff1077. The result is stored in RAM ffff1fab and ffff24e1; in FUN_00038d44, saved ffff24e1 is tested for zero while bit 0x40 of RAM ffff4185 is set, and a true test is one condition for setting bit 0x02 of RAM ffff24bc. The physical subsystem is unknown. The lookup result is copied to ffff1fab and ffff24e1; a shown consumer exists only for ffff24e1. The map is updated when bit 0x40 of ffff4185 is clear, while the zero test of the saved byte acts when the bit is set, so the dependence crosses calls through RAM. All eight cells equal 90: the stock lookup always yields 90, and target disjunct ffff24e1 == 0 is false after the map write. This does not prove that the entire branch is unreachable because the bit-setting condition has other disjuncts. A nontrivial scale is not proven. Index: Implicit uniform eight-point axis over x = u8 RAM ffff1077: for x &lt; 224, index i = floor(x/32), fraction = (x-i*32)/32, and map[i]..map[i+1] are linearly interpolated; for x &gt;= 224, map[7] is selected. Output trace: 00012a9a -&gt; 00038e6e -&gt; 00038e74 -&gt; 00026370 -&gt; (00026a80 -&gt; 00026740 for x &lt; 224; map[7] for x &gt;= 224) -&gt; 00038e78 -&gt; 00038e84 -&gt; ffff24e1 -&gt; FUN_00038d44: (ffff4185 &amp; 0x40) != 0 &amp;&amp; ffff24e1 == 0 -&gt; ffff24bc |= 0x02. The same RAM copy is populated by path 00012a9a -&gt; 0002cfc0 -&gt; 0002cfd2 -&gt; ffff24e1. Result disposition: inline_comparison; Result target: RAM ffff24e1 in FUN_00038d44: inline test ffff24e1 == 0 under selector ffff4185 &amp; 0x40; a true disjunct participates in setting bit 0x02 of RAM ffff24bc. A mirrored result write is in RAM ffff1fab.</description>
