  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xB5C8" flags="0x0">
    <title>Three-Factor Product Multiplier B - raw u8 (0x12AC2)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12AC2; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. One of three unsigned byte factors in a normalized composition: the lookup result is multiplied by two other byte results, and the combined product is divided by 16384 and saturated to 255. Both accessors execute the same path. The interpolated value is written to ffff183a, read within the same accessor, and enters a product with two other unsigned byte results. The product is shifted right by a total of 14 bits, capped at 255, and written to ffff15c6. Code does not establish the physical purpose of the factor. The shift normalizes the combined product but, without independent scales for the other factors, does not define a separate physical map scale, so values remain raw. Index: 1D-8 uint8 with an implicit uniform axis: index = min(floor(input/32), 7), fraction = (input mod 32)/32, input = uint8 from ffff10f5; for input &gt;= 224, cell 7 is selected; otherwise adjacent cells are linearly interpolated. Output trace: 00081730(00012ac2) -&gt; 0008173c -&gt; 00026370 -&gt; 00026a80 -&gt; 00026aac/00026aae -&gt; 00026740 -&gt; 00081740 -&gt; 00081746 -&gt; ffff183a -&gt; 00081768 -&gt; 0008176e -&gt; 00081774 -&gt; 00081778/0008177a/0008177c/0008177e -&gt; 00081780/00081786 -&gt; 00081788 -&gt; ffff15c6; paired path: 00081f62(00012ac2) -&gt; 00081f6e -&gt; 00026370 -&gt; 00026a80 -&gt; 00026aac/00026aae -&gt; 00026740 -&gt; 00081f72 -&gt; 00081f78 -&gt; ffff183a -&gt; 00081f9a -&gt; 00081fa0 -&gt; 00081fa6 -&gt; 00081faa/00081fac/00081fae/00081fb0 -&gt; 00081fb2/00081fb8 -&gt; 00081fbc -&gt; ffff15c6. Result disposition: consumer; Result target: ffff183a -&gt; 0008152a/0008176e; ffff183a -&gt; 00081d74/00081fa0.</description>
