  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x2341" flags="0x0">
    <title>State 2 Hold Gate Table - raw u8 (0x12ADA)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12ADA; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Implicit 1D table of a zero/nonzero permission to hold internal state 2. The lookup result is written to u8[ffff254b] and tested for zero on the state-2 branch: a nonzero result enables comparison u8[ffff1188] &gt; 100; if the comparison is true, state 2 is retained, otherwise state 1 is selected. The artifact does not identify the physical subsystem. All 8 cells in the stock map equal 6, so the lookup always yields a nonzero result and effectively enables test u8[ffff1188] &gt; 100. The write and read occur in 00038618 but belong to different states; ffff254b has no external readers. The implicit map has no separate axis array. Index: implicit 1D-8: x = u8[ffff107f]; for x &lt; 224, i = floor(x/32), Q0.16 fraction q = (x mod 32)*2048, interpolation of map[i]..map[i+1]; for x &gt;= 224, map[7] is returned. Output trace: 00038a68 -&gt; 00038a6e -&gt; 00026370 -&gt; 00026a80 -&gt; 00026740 -&gt; 00038a74 -&gt; ffff254b -&gt; 00038ad6 -&gt; 00038ad8; zero -&gt; 00038ada -&gt; 00038b7c, nonzero -&gt; 00038adc -&gt; 00038ae2 -&gt; 00038ae4 -&gt; 00038ae6. Result disposition: inline_comparison; Result target: RAM ffff254b; consumer 00038618; site 00038ad8.</description>
