  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x41C3" flags="0x0">
    <title>Bit 7 Hold State Table - raw u8 (0x12AFA)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12AFA; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Eight-node byte-state table. When bit 6 of ffff2462 is set, the lookup writes the result to ffff254d and sets bit 7 of ffff246c. On the branch with bit 6 clear, saved byte ffff254d is tested for zero: zero clears bit 7 of ffff246c, while nonzero preserves it. All cells equal 6, so this map's result is always 6 and is handled as nonzero. The physical subsystem and engineering unit are not established: ffff254d has no external readers and the catalog shape is ambiguous. All eight cells equal 6, so interpolation and the terminal branch return 6; this proves a nonzero state and branch behavior but not the physical name of the quantity. Index: x=uint8(ffff106f). For x&lt;224: i=floor(x/32), q=(x-32*i)*2048 in Q0.16, and cell[i] and cell[i+1] are interpolated. For x&gt;=224, cell[7] is returned. The axis is implicit, with no separate Axis claim. Output trace: 00012afa -&gt; 00043afe -&gt; 00043b04 -&gt; 00026370 -&gt; 00026a80 -&gt; {00026aac,00026aae} -&gt; 00026740 -&gt; 00043b08 -&gt; ffff254d; subsequent state read: ffff254d -&gt; 00043b10 -&gt; 00043b12 -&gt; 00043b14 -&gt; 00043b1a. Value 6 does not follow zero branch 00043b18. Result disposition: inline_comparison; Result target: site 00043b12 through ffff254d. Static diagnostic context: Engine Coolant Temperature [code, homologous_community, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
