  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x8544" flags="0x0">
    <title>Channel 0 Signed Additive Term (x-128) (0x12E72)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12E72; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Eight-point uint8 table of a centered additive term for channel 0. The lookup is indexed by RAM ffff106f; interpolated byte x is stored in ffff1a7b. The accessor calculates RAM[ffff16e8] + (x-128)*65536, saturates the result to range 0..16777215, and writes ffff1a9c; FUN 000be814 reads this slot when param_1=0. The physical subsystem is unknown. Code proves the centered term and its path. Before saturation, A = RAM[ffff16e8] + (x-128)*65536; saturation to 0..16777215 applies to composite A and is not included in the invertible map scale. One whole scale unit equals 65536 internal counts; round trip is exact: (x-128)+128=x for bytes 0..255. The "Output association" section row stating that there is no sink contradicts the listing: result r0 is copied to r2 at 000be792, written to ffff1a7b at 000be798, and then the derived quantity is written to ffff1a9c at 000be7b6 and read by 000be814 for param_1=0. Axis 00011bdb belongs only to adjacent explicit maps and is not included in the claim. Index: implicit 1D-8: RAM byte ffff106f is passed in r5 to wrapper 00026370; for a value &lt;224, kernel 00026a80 selects adjacent uint8 cells and 00026740 performs unsigned linear interpolation; for a value &gt;=224, the wrapper selects element 7. Output trace: 00012e72 -&gt; 000be786 -&gt; 000be78e/00026370 -&gt; 00026a80 -&gt; 00026aac,00026aae -&gt; 00026740 -&gt; 000be792 -&gt; 000be798/ffff1a7b; 000be79e -&gt; 000be7a0 -&gt; 000be7a2 -&gt; 000be7a4 -&gt; 000be7a6,000be7aa,000be7ae,000be7ac,000be7b2 -&gt; 000be7b6/ffff1a9c -&gt; 000be814(param_1=0). Result disposition: consumer; Result target: FUN 000be814 through RAM ffff1a9c when param_1=0; raw copy in RAM ffff1a7b. Static diagnostic context: Engine Coolant Temperature [code, homologous_community, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
