  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x69C3" flags="0x0">
    <title>Conditional Paired State Value B - raw u8 (0x12F06)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12F06; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Conditionally selected 8-bit table for a paired write: on the update branch in 000bdc66, previous values ffff1a1e and ffff25ee form part of the gate; when 00012f06 is selected, uint8 ffff106f serves as the lookup index and the result is written to both registers. The physical meaning of the pair and the exact change to ffff2326 are not claimed. On the update branch in 000bdc66, previous values ffff1a1e != 0 and ffff25ee == 0 enter the gate before the lookup. The selector chooses 00012f06 instead of 00012efe; all eight cells in 00012f06 equal 5, so the current calibration returns 5 regardless of index. The physical subsystem, value unit, mechanism that clears ffff25ee, and exact change to ffff2326 are unknown. Index: implicit 1D-8 by uint8 ffff106f: linear interpolation of adjacent bytes for x&lt;224, element[7] for x&gt;=224. Output trace: 00012f06 -&gt; 000bde7a/000bde82 -&gt; 00026370 -&gt; 00026a80 -&gt; 00026aac/00026aae -&gt; 00026740 -&gt; 000bde86 -&gt; 000bde8c/000bde94 -&gt; ffff1a1e/ffff25ee; before the next write, previous values ffff1a1e and ffff25ee are tested in the 000bdc66 gate. Result disposition: consumer; Result target: RAM ffff1a1e and ffff25ee; consumer function 000bdc66. Static diagnostic context: Engine Coolant Temperature [code, homologous_community, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
