  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x6DE5" flags="0x0">
    <title>Conditional Signed State Value (x-128) (0x13016)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x13016; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Eight-point uint8 table of a centered signed value. The lookup result is decoded as x-128, constrained to range -16..15 when bit 0x40 of RAM ffff249f is set, or replaced with zero otherwise, then written as a byte to RAM ffff15c8. The physical quantity is unknown. All 8 cells equal 128, so the lookup yields 128, decoding yields 0, the clamp does not change the result, and with the enable bit clear the same 0 is written. The artifact has no external readers of ffff15c8; this remains a write rather than a proven dead branch. The physical quantity is unknown. The scale applies to the value before the clamp. Numeric round trip: 0 -&gt; -128 -&gt; 0; 128 -&gt; 0 -&gt; 128; 255 -&gt; 127 -&gt; 255. Index: Implicit uniform eight-point axis. q=min((u16 RAM[ffff1152] / 8),255). For q&lt;224, the kernel obtains the adjacent uint8-cell index with five right shifts of q and passes the cells to unsigned linear interpolation with a Q0.16 fraction; for q&gt;=224, the wrapper returns cell 7. Bit 0x40 of RAM[ffff249f] enables the lookup. Output trace: q&lt;224: 00013016 -&gt; 00076404 -&gt; 00076408 -&gt; 00026370 -&gt; 00026a80 -&gt; 00026aac/00026aae -&gt; 00026740 -&gt; 0007640c -&gt; 00076410 -&gt; 00076412 -&gt; 00076416/00076422 -&gt; 00076434 -&gt; ffff15c8; q&gt;=224: 00013016+7 -&gt; 00026370 -&gt; 0007640c -&gt; 00076410 -&gt; 00076412 -&gt; 00076416/00076422 -&gt; 00076434 -&gt; ffff15c8. Result disposition: writes; Result target: RAM ffff15c8, byte store site 00076434.</description>
