  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x8A29" flags="0x0">
    <title>State Decrease Step B - raw u16 (0x14314)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x14314; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. 1D table of a decrement step for RAM state ffff17c0. During a descending update, the lookup is compared with current ffff17c0: if current &gt;= lookup and the calculated target &lt;= current - lookup, current - lookup is written; if current &lt; lookup, the state is zeroed. Otherwise the higher calculated target is retained. The physical subsystem is unknown. The map is selected by the branch that adds 0x10 to base 00014304 when a calculated 8-bit selector lies outside the range of two bytes at 00008ace. The lookup result is not written as an independent quantity: it is consumed inside 00074e4e while limiting a descending update of ffff17c0; external readers of derived ffff23fc are not used as evidence for target-map semantics. The map has no explicit ROM axis, so axes is empty. Index: 1D-8 with an implicit axis. Coordinate r5 is formed as saturating uint16(RAM_ffff1210 &lt;&lt; 7): for RAM_ffff1210 &gt;= 0x0200, 0xffff is used. For coordinate &lt; 0xe000, wrapper 000263d8 interpolates adjacent uint16 values through 00026a60/00026740; otherwise it returns element 7 at offset +0x0e. Output trace: 00014314 -&gt; site 00074f30 -&gt; site 00074f36 -&gt; 000263d8 -&gt; [00026a60 -&gt; 00026740 | direct +0x0e return] -&gt; site 00074f48 -&gt; site 00074f6c -&gt; site 00074f70 -&gt; 00074e4e -&gt; ffff17c0 -&gt; ffff23fc. Result disposition: inline_comparison; Result target: site 00074f70.</description>
