  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x4D69" flags="0x0">
    <title>Rounded UQ0.16 Threshold Coefficient (0x15082)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x15082; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Eight-point implicit table of an unsigned UQ0.16 coefficient. The lookup result scales the lookup result of map 00015062; rounded product/65536 forms a local 16-bit comparison threshold. All 8 cells equal 0xffff, but constant content is not used as semantic evidence. The claim is based on trace lookup -&gt; fixed-point multiplication -&gt; derived threshold -&gt; comparison. The physical names of the indexing quantity and compared parameter are not proven. The inverse pair is exact in the raw domain: for r=0..65535, round((r/65536)*65536)=r. Index: v is selected by branching before the lookup: with bit 0x80 at 00008b3f clear, U16_BE[ffff10d2] is selected; on the other branch, v is formed from U16_BE[ffff1016] by multiplication by 0x280 and byte swapping at 0007316e..00073196. At 00073198..000731aa, q=sat_u16(v&lt;&lt;7) is calculated. For q&lt;0xe000, wrapper 000263d8 transfers control to implicit kernel 00026a60 for linear interpolation of 8 adjacent U16 cells through 00026740; for q&gt;=0xe000, the wrapper returns the last cell map[7] at offset +0x0e. There is no separate axis array in ROM. Output trace: On the path that reaches 000731b2: BE U16 cells of map 00015082 -&gt; wrapper 000263d8 -&gt; implicit kernel 00026a60 -&gt; linear finisher 00026740 -&gt; r0; 000731b6 zero-extends the result, 000731b8 multiplies it by the zero-extended lookup result of map 00015062 in r14, 000731be adds 0x8000, and 000731c0 extracts the high 16 bits into r4. 000731c8 writes the derived threshold to ffff1734, then 000731ee compares the current value in r5 with r4; the comparison result participates in updating bit 0x04 at ffff2488. The direct lookup result from 00015082 has no separate RAM sink. Result disposition: inline_comparison; Result target: 000731b8 (direct arithmetic consumer) -&gt; ffff1734 (derived threshold) -&gt; 000731ee (comparison).</description>
