  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x4BD7" flags="0x0">
    <title>Saturating Internal State Load - raw u16 (0x15330)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x15330; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Eight-point uint16 table of a value for conditional internal-state loading: lookup result x is converted as min(x*256,65535), written to ffff32b8, and its high byte is written to ffff413f. On the alternate path, this state is compared with a step quantity and reduced with saturation toward zero. The physical subsystem and physical units are unknown: root FUN_00066186 has no call sites, and the artifact has no external readers of the RAM values. Code confidence applies only to narrow operational semantics. The map is flat, so in this ROM the lookup always yields 20; runtime conversion produces 5120 (0x1400), while 20 is written to ffff413f. Saturating conversion min(x*256,65535) is not claimed as a scale because it lacks an exact inverse pair. Index: implicit 1D-8: q=min(uint16[ffff40c6]*128,65535); for q&lt;57344, the kernel performs linear interpolation of adjacent uint16 values; for q&gt;=57344, the wrapper selects element 7. Output trace: 000661be [delay slot 000661c0 sets r4=00015330] -&gt; 000263d8 -&gt; 00026a60 -&gt; 00026740 -&gt; return to 000661c2 -&gt; 000661c6 -&gt; 000661ca/000661ce -&gt; 000661d6 -&gt; ffff32b8 -&gt; high-byte extraction in 00066186 -&gt; ffff413f; on the alternate path, ffff32b8 -&gt; 000661f4 -&gt; comparison and subtraction in 00066186 -&gt; ffff32b8. Result disposition: writes; Result target: RAM ffff32b8 at site 000661d6; RAM ffff413f receives the high byte of ffff32b8 in FUN_00066186.</description>
