  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x5943" flags="0x0">
    <title>Latched Zero Condition Table - raw u8 (0x12026)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12026; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Eight-point table of a raw byte condition: the lookup result indexed by ffff1070 is conditionally latched in ffff42a8; ffff42a8 is then tested for equality to zero inside 00082c8a and, together with control flags, determines whether bit 1 of ffff41d2 is set or cleared. All eight cells equal 0, so lookup always returns 0 in this ROM; flat contents alone do not prove semantics. Code proves narrow operational semantics of a zero condition. Writing the result and the enabling zero test are mutually exclusive within one call, so the effective zero test may use a value previously latched in ffff42a8. On the alternate path, a ROM constant is written to ffff42a8 instead of the map result. The physical subsystem and physical name of the quantity are unknown. Index: Implicit uniform 1D-8 indexing by x=uint8 RAM[ffff1070]. When x&lt;224: i=floor(x/32), q=(x-32*i)*2048 in Q0.16, with interpolation between map[i] and map[i+1]. When x&gt;=224, map[7] is selected. Output trace: ffff1070 -&gt; site 00083868 (x in r5); 00012026 -&gt; site 0008386a (r4) -&gt; site 0008386e -&gt; 00026370. When x &lt; 224: 00026a80 -&gt; cell reads at 00026aac/00026aae -&gt; 00026740; when x &gt;= 224: direct cell 0001202d. Return r0 -&gt; site 00083872 (r12) -&gt; conditional write to ffff42a8 -&gt; test ffff42a8 == 0 inside 00082c8a -&gt; bit 1 of ffff41d2. ffff42a8 has no external readers. Result disposition: inline_comparison; Result target: RAM ffff42a8; zero test in function 00082c8a; the condition contributes to updating RAM ffff41d2 bit 1.</description>
