    <title>Interpolated State Byte - raw u8 (0x12E1A)</title>
    <description>Exact JK08A. Address 0x12E1A; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Interpolated 1D table of 16 uint8 elements indexed by unsigned byte input ffff106f. For input &gt;=0xf0, the last element is selected; otherwise the result is linearly interpolated between adjacent elements. The resulting byte is stored without arithmetic conversion in ffff351b and copied by consumer 000c5558 to ffff3af5. Interpolated 1D table of 16 uint8 elements indexed by unsigned byte input ffff106f. For input &gt;=0xf0, the last element is selected; otherwise the result is linearly interpolated between adjacent elements. The resulting byte is stored without arithmetic conversion in ffff351b and copied by consumer 000c5558 to ffff3af5. Result disposition: consumer. Result target: 000c5558 (R ffff351b, W ffff3af5). Machine trace: 000793ea: r4=00012e1a; 000793ec and delay slot 000793f4: byte from ffff106f is zero-extended into r5; 000793f2: call 00026388. For input &gt;=0xf0, the wrapper returns the last element at base+0x0f; otherwise it transfers control to kernel 00026a84. Branch 00026aaa..00026ab2 reads adjacent elements through mov.b and zero-extends them, then 00026ab4 passes y0/y1 and the Q0.16 fraction to finisher 00026740. The finisher performs unsigned linear interpolation with a result between y0 and y1. 000793f6 moves r0 to r2 without arithmetic; 00079400 writes the low byte to ffff351b. In 000c5558, expression *(ffff3ab5+0x40)=*(ffff28f8+0x0c23) copies byte ffff351b directly to ffff3af5.</description>
